Package: maffect
Title: GWAS Plots with Effect Sizes, Allele Frequency and Genes
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
    person("Andrew", "Elmore", , "andrew.elmore@bristol.ac.uk", role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0003-0292-447X"))
Description: Plots for genome-wide association study (GWAS) results that
    show effect size and allele frequency alongside significance, for
    studies with many loci and rare variants. The Manhattan plot adds an
    aligned track with each locus's effect size and confidence interval,
    colours variants by minor allele frequency, and labels loci with their
    nearest gene (or any label you supply). Companion plots show effect size
    against allele frequency with the study's detection limit, a volcano
    plot, a regional plot with linkage disequilibrium (from 'LDlink' or your
    own table), Miami and forest plots to compare two studies, and a QQ plot
    by frequency class. Output from 'PLINK', 'REGENIE', 'SAIGE', 'BOLT-LMM',
    'METAL' and GWAS-SSF files is recognised, and tens of millions of
    variants plot in seconds. Lead variants whose effect disagrees with their
    own case and control allele frequencies can be flagged. Built on
    'ggplot2'.
URL: https://github.com/andrew-e/maffect
